# Coding Standards

Follow SOLID principles.

Single Responsibility:
Each class has one responsibility.

Open Closed:
Extend functionality without modifying core classes.

Liskov Substitution:
Interfaces must be replaceable by implementations.

Interface Segregation:
Prefer small focused interfaces.

Dependency Inversion:
Depend on interfaces instead of concrete classes.

Never:

Put business logic in controllers.

Query database inside controllers.

Mix validation with business logic.

Validation must use Form Requests.

Authorization must use Policies.

